{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/965647-supernatural-merit","id":965647,"title":"Supernatural merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T07:03:57-07:00","id":965647,"title":"Supernatural merit","content":"I am running a game where are some players are adapting supernatural abilities one of my players would like to adapt a ability to know when someone is lying.<br /> <br /> What should the Merit rating be three or four or five dots and any suggestions on details other than just knowing when someone lies perhaps a drawback","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:58:12-07:00","id":965680,"title":"","content":"The book Second Sight contains all kinds of supernatural and semi-supernatural merits like that, psychic powers, you name it. It's a nWoD book, not CofD but easy to convert I'm sure. DruvethruRPG has the PDF for $15.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:36:19-07:00","id":965700,"title":"","content":"Almost all the powers in the Second Sight Book have been converted into the the CofD book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:53:20-07:00","id":965707,"title":"","content":"Just whether someone is lying? I'd say 1 or 2 dots. Telepathy allows for more detailed information than Lying/not-Lying and that's rated at 3 dots. Roll is probably Wits + Empathy (or Subterfuge) opposed by Composure. Maybe target an individual for a Scene for one Willpower, or affect everything overheard for the entire Scene? Or cut the WP cost - it <i>is</i> a rather limited ability.<br /> <br /> Just remember that most Supernatural Merits come with a Drawback for use. Triggering when you don't want it to and/or giving you some condition like Spooked or Paranoid would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-08-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:14:56-07:00","id":966078,"title":"","content":"I would say a variable-cost merit. A lot of them are.<br /> At 1 dot you may spend a willpower to &quot;turn it on&quot; for a scene. For 2 or 3 dots its just always on, no need to activate or anything.<br /> It should have some representation that you can describe, hopefully a macabre one (like bugs pouring from their mouths as they speak lies, I think this was a vampire ritual somewhere) so you don't have to break the scene ( &quot;No, she had nothing to do with that, she says and roaches pour from her mouth, dropping onto her plate before scuttling away&quot; sounds a lot better at the table than &quot;No, she had nothing to do with that, and you know she's lying&quot;)<br /> As Vent0 said, they usually have a drawback, so maybe one related to seeing gruesome stuff, or as was suggested, Paranoid is great.<br /> <br /> But as was mentioned, it's not that spectacular. A mage at my table as Prime and with it he can do this (and does practically all the time.) It's not nearly as useful in play as it would first appear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:11:17-07:00","id":966143,"title":"","content":"You do realize that telling when someone is lying is one of the basic functions of Aura Reading, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:28:03-07:00","id":966238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/965647-supernatural-merit?p=966143#post966143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that telling when someone is lying is one of the basic functions of Aura Reading, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Aura Reading lets you ask questions of the target, including &quot;Is your character telling the truth?&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:45:02-07:00","id":966321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/965647-supernatural-merit?p=966238#post966238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This. Aura Reading lets you ask questions of the target, including &quot;Is your character telling the truth?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Aura Reading is two dots. That can serve, unless they don't want all the other abilities, in which cases a one dot merit that just has the lie detection might serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T06:45:34-07:00","id":966729,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys for the feed back! I'm thinking we'll go with 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Should have mentioned before, the character is demonic, not a lucifuge, but demon born and the ability was supposed to develope out of the fact that you can't tell if a demon is lying backwards to apply that they're good at spotting lies.<br /> <br /> So for a simple character cannot be lied, with no roll. Ya'll recommend 2 dots? Maybe 3 if there is no willpower point activation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:16:10-07:00","id":966743,"title":"","content":"3 sounds about right for no cost no drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:48:44-07:00","id":967403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/965647-supernatural-merit?p=966729#post966729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys for the feed back! I'm thinking we'll go with 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Should have mentioned before, the character is demonic, not a lucifuge, but demon born and the ability was supposed to develope out of the fact that you can't tell if a demon is lying backwards to apply that they're good at spotting lies.<br /> <br /> So for a simple character cannot be lied, with no roll. Ya'll recommend 2 dots? Maybe 3 if there is no willpower point activation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If they are Offspring or a Fractal, why not just give them one or more of the various truth-telling or divulge-information Embeds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}